  "description": "The double-count P1 fix. Reservation A is exposed then committed: commit(exposed) decrements exposedTotal as it increments cumulativeCommitted, so cumulativeConsumed stays 6, not 12 — the amount moves terms, it is not counted twice. Then reservation B fills the rest of the hourly cap and is exposed; a third reserve C is refused, proving the exposed B occupies the cap exactly once next to the committed A (committed 6 + exposed 4 + 1 > 10). The invariant cumulativeConsumed = cumulativeCommitted + exposedTotal + reservedOnly holds at every snapshot.",
